    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d146-a1">

                <pb facs="0244" n="198" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v02/pg198"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of War</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Crowell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to President
                        Wilson </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 10, 1918.</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: In reply to your letter
                    of October 7th<anchor n="25" xml:id="d146-f1"/> inclosing a letter from the
                    Secretary of State of October 5th, in which it is proposed that the subjects of
                    Turkey, for the purposes of the administration of the Draft Act, be treated as
                    though they were alien enemies, I have the honor to inform you that I agree
                    fully with the Secretary of State as to the advisability of taking the action he
                    proposes.</p>
                <p>Cordially yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Benedict Crowell</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
